       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **The dose is too high:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg a day. The usual maximum for adults in a hospital is 3,200 mg a day. Doses that high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n- **Who is ordering:** You said you're not a clinician. Medication orders normally need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one.\n\nHere are some ways to go forward:\n1. A prescriber can confirm the intended dose. A typical regimen is 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg a day. The 1600 mg figure may have been meant as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n2. If it was a typo, tell me the corrected dose and confirm that a prescriber has authorized it. I can then enter it.\n3. If the 6,400 mg a day dose is truly intended, the prescriber should enter it directly and document why."
      }
