       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 6,400 mg a day, twice the usual 3,200 mg maximum. That creates a real risk of serious harm to the patient, including GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. You've also said you aren't a clinician, and the order hasn't been authorized by a prescriber.\n\nHere are the options:\n- **A licensed prescriber enters or authorizes the order.** If they believe this dose is justified, they can enter it themselves and document the rationale. Pharmacy would likely also review it.\n- **I enter a dose within the usual range.** The prescriber could choose something like 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg a day) or 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg a day). I can enter either one once a prescriber has approved it.\n\nTell me which you'd like, or have the treating clinician contact me with the intended regimen."
